 Cafe","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Food, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"_C7QiQQc47AOEv4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"Food","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"LkCFcD-5QyNIUnEfO78npw","review_id":"-SdjnK-lTbMtV-Kw35IcRg","date":"2012-04-05T16:17:36","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9466161727905273,"text_excerpt":"I had a really great meal at Chartres House. It was a very cool space with an interesting back story. The drink selections were good - lots of variety and everything we tried was on point. We had fried alligator as an appetizer - a first for all of us - and it was pretty tasty. An interesting texture and the taste was a little different than what I expected but still good. I had trouble deciding what to go with for dinner so I went with the \"Taste of New Orleans\" (gumbo, jambalaya, and red beans & rice). Amazing! I loved all three dishes and left very satisfied. The tabasco wings were also quite good. Overall, a reasonably priced and very satisfying meal. Worth a trip."},{"business_id":"LkCFcD-5QyNIUnEfO78npw","review_id":"BxLk7MjubsuYFsBCR_AyFw","date":"2017-03-19T00:58:57","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9452427625656128,"text_excerpt":"My friends and I enjoyed a pretty good dinner here while we were in New Orleans. We went in at around 6:30pm, and the place wasn't super busy (uncommon for the French Quarter at that time). They have a great selection of local beers! They have IPAs, stouts, etc. all on draft (I think they had 15 draft beers), and others in bottles and cans. Our meals were all pretty good, except the crawfish in the crawfish etouffee were absolutely tiny and a blue/gray color that worries us. They have a lot of fried food, but classics like their jumbalaya and gumbo are great choices. The New Orleans tasting trio is a great choice if you want to try a few of their classics. My friend who was a vegetarian h..."},{"business_id":"LkCFcD-5QyNIUnEfO78npw","review_id":"JRuEyasyFgPb2JzdiZPOvQ","date":"2009-08-09T07:32:36","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9305877685546875,"text_excerpt":"This restaurant has some of the best food I've ever ate. And I have had some good food but let me just say that Chartres House Cafe is truly a must! Okay, so my girlfriend and I are visiting New Orleans for the weekend and of course, we've had a few drinks to say the least. After walking for 2 hours on a Vampire Tour, we stirred up quite the appetite only to find ourselves lost in New Orleans! To our luck or perhaps it was fate, Chartres House Cafe was open and lively filled with people. The restaurant itself was dark. Dark wood, minimal lighting, kind of like a lodge or better said, a cabin-type ambiance. This didn't bother us much as it was already late, about 11PM. The service was grea..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"LkCFcD-5QyNIUnEfO78npw","photo_id":"EfLty0MH33OoQBqGsPwcvg","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/EfLty0MH33OoQBqGsPwcvg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.887804388999939},{"business_id":"LkCFcD-5